import MassGap.Transfer  -- the transfer operator the tree did not have, which is what `hdecay` would have to be a statement about. Reflect supplied the reflection; this supplies the operator theory it is FOR. The Wilson reflection form <F,G> = <(F.theta).G> is defined and PROVED symmetric (from expect_reflect_invariant plus theta^2 = id) and normalised (<1,1> = 1); its POSITIVITY is reflection positivity and is carried as the field ReflForm.form_nonneg so nothing can assume it silently -- no ReflForm is built from the Wilson measure IN THIS FILE. One is built elsewhere: LogConvex.wilsonReflForm discharges form_nonneg from LogConvex.pairing_nonneg, which holds over the whole half-space observable module at EVERY real β with no sign hypothesis, so the positivity this file leaves open is proved there. From any form that has it: Cauchy-Schwarz, the null space is a submodule, and the quotient carries a genuine InnerProductSpace R via InnerProductSpace.Core (definite holds by construction). A contractive time translation descends to it, is self-adjoint, fixes the vacuum at eigenvalue exactly 1 and has operator norm at most 1 -- all normalisation, no gap. In finite dimension the eigen-expansion of <v,T^k v> has square weights, giving Spectral.PeriodicSpectralForm. Building the object at once shows hdecay is FALSE read over the full spectrum: one_le_of_eigenvalues_le says a bound r on every eigenvalue forces r >= 1, because the vacuum is a unit eigenvector at 1 -- so the gap statement is about the spectrum on Omega-perp, the connected correlator. Foundation-only.
import MassGap.VortexFamily  -- item 1 of the Clay finalisation: hM discharged. VortexCount's junction consumed hM : forall k, 3^k <= M k as a hypothesis, and SurfaceEmbed could only count inside a family V a CALLER supplied. Theorem 7.1's N(A) is not a supplied family -- it is the number of CLOSED surfaces of area A through a FIXED plaquette -- so the containment had to stop being a hypothesis and become a check against a definition. It is: IsClosedSurface is WilsonHypercubic.bd (the Wilson holonomy's own boundary map) with orientations dropped, every link in an even number of plaquettes; plaqSurface_closed proves the embedded surfaces satisfy it by transporting CubeClosed.edge_parity_all, with links along time or off the time-zero slice even by being carried by none; vortexFamily is then DEFINED as the closed surfaces of area 4k+6 through basePlaq, and three_pow_le_vortexCount is 3^k <= its cardinality with NO hypothesis at all -- boxOf k = k+3 is the successor of the largest coordinate the construction produces, not a choice. junction_of_vortexFamily is the junction with hM gone, resting on hdual alone. Foundational only.
