import MassGap.CubeBranch  -- the entropy floor RAISED above (1/4) log 3, by counting a strictly richer subfamily of the same closed surfaces. Floor+CubeArea count DIRECTED CUBE-PATHS: 3^k of them, each bounding a distinct closed surface of area exactly 4k+6, giving kappa_0 >= (1/4) log 3 = 0.2746531. Paths are not the only surfaces of that area and kappa_0 is a limsup over ALL closed surfaces, so a richer subfamily bounds the SAME quantity from below by more. The family here is a path (the SPINE) of (d+1)k+1 steps carrying ONE extra cube per block of d+1 steps, at one of d positions in the block, on an axis FORCED to avoid both the spine direction at its own index and the next one. Every cube but the origin then has exactly one face-neighbour below it, so the configuration is a TREE and the SAME double count CubeArea.boundary_card_of_shared makes -- already stated there for an arbitrary Finset Cube -- gives |dC| = 6n - 2(n-1) = 4n+2, the path's own area law at n = k+1. eq_of_boundaryFaces_eq frees CubeArea's surface-injectivity from the path entirely: mem_boundaryFaces_iff_floor decides membership on the floor and mem_boundaryFaces_iff_xor propagates it, so ANY two configurations with the same boundary are equal and any family is counted by its surfaces as soon as it is counted by its cubes. branched_surfaces_count_and_area: 3^((d+1)k+1) * d^k distinct surfaces, each of area exactly 4((d+2)k+2)+2. The density is ((d+1)log3 + log d)/(4(d+2)), which beats (1/4)log3 exactly when log d > log 3, i.e. d > 3 -- and d = 3 reproduces the path floor EXACTLY (3^(d+1)*d = 3^(d+2) over the same area), which is the negative control. Best at d = 10: kappa_0 >= (11 log 3 + log 10)/48 = 0.2997358. Closedness transports free (CubeClosed.edge_parity_all is already general); CONNECTEDNESS of the new boundaries is NOT proved here -- CubeConnected's descent is written for the one-cube-per-layer path -- so this raises the counted floor and does not yet replace CubeConnected's input to Vo