import MassGap.LogConvex  -- LOG-CONVEXITY OF THE LAG CORRELATION IN THE LAG, constant one, the first coupling-free ratio inequality in the tree: corrClay (e1 + e2)^2 <= corrClay (e1 + e1) * corrClay (e2 + e2) at every EVEN extent, every REAL coupling and every pair of lags strictly below half the extent. Reflection positivity is a statement about a bilinear form and the tree had only its diagonal; ActionSplit.pairing_nonneg_of_local was already quantified over observables, so the diagonal holds on a whole vector space -- localObs, the bounded measurable functions reading one half-space plus the plane -- and wilsonReflForm is the first Transfer.ReflForm ever built from the Wilson measure, every field proved: symmetry from the measure-preserving involution plus a plane weight the reflection does not move, bilinearity from the integral, form_nonneg from the three-block weld. Transfer.ReflForm.cauchy_schwarz then reads the off-diagonal against the two diagonals. THE CONSTANT IS ONE BECAUSE THE GEOMETRY MAKES IT ONE: all three pairings come from ONE reflection at ONE plane and share ONE partition function, so nothing is left over to be a constant. integrand_eq_paired_pair is ActionSplit.integrand_eq_paired with the two plaquettes kept apart -- its proof never needed them equal, the mirror identity actPlus o Theta = actMinus is about the ACTION. EW_plaqE_pair_shift is translation invariance derived FROM the reflection (<phi_P phi_Q> = <phi_0 phi_{P-Q}>, one application of expect_reflect_invariant at constant P, both plaquettes moving under the same map), so no separate translation symmetry was needed. TWO HYPOTHESES THE ODD-LAG WORK NEEDED ARE ABSENT HERE. 0 <= beta is not required: this runs entirely on the even-lag weld, a conditional square against a strictly positive Boltzmann weight that never reads the coupling's sign. The odd-lag link reflection is not required either, though the cross lag e1 + e2 may be ODD -- an odd lag reached as an OFF-DIAGONAL pairing under a