import MassGap.MomentShape  -- CIRCLE SYMMETRY OF THE LAG CORRELATION, PROVED: corrHyper_neg gives rho(-d) = rho(d) at EVERY extent and EVERY real coupling with no hypothesis, from LogConvex.EW_plaqE_pair_shift at P = 0 plus the lag-independence of the one-point term. wilsonCorrAt_circLag_congr is the useful form -- the correlation reads the lag ONLY through Moment.circLag -- which is exactly what Complete's docstrings record as ASSUMED ("no theorem in the tree asserts it of wilsonCorrAt, corrClay, corrHyper or wilsonCorrConn"); circLag is BUILT as if it held and now it is a theorem. THE SHAPE LOG-CONVEXITY EARNS, and only that: at even extent with m >= 3, corrClay_even_antitone puts rho restricted to the EVEN lags non-increasing in circLag (log-convex in c on g c = rho(2c) from the decomposition (c-1)+(c+1) = 2c, symmetric about m/2 by the above, and a convex function with equal endpoints falls on its first half), and corrClay_odd_le bounds each odd lag ABOVE by its two even neighbours. A NO-GO ON THE REST: every right-hand lag the log-convexity produces is 2e, hence EVEN, so odd_scaling_admissible proves the premise set is closed under scaling rho at the ODD lags alone by any t in [0,1] -- nonnegativity, circle symmetry and log-convexity all survive -- and therefore NO theorem from these premises can lower-bound an odd lag. circLag = 1 is odd, so monotonicity of the WHOLE profile in circLag is not merely unproved but underivable, and not_antitone_circLag_of_shape exhibits a conforming profile at extent eight that dips at circle distance three and rises again at four. shape_wilsonCorrAt confirms the Wilson correlation satisfies exactly that premise set, so the no-go is about the real object. NO BOUND ON substrateRatio IS CLAIMED OR PROVED: at extent four the constraints leave the antipodal point mass at exactly 1/4, and the best case this shape could describe is the flat read, which Substrate.flatRead_exceeds_ceiling already proves is above the ceiling at every ape