import MassGap.LogDerivNoGo  -- B5'S RECORDED TARGET IS REFUTED TWICE, AND THE L1 TARGET IS NOT. CosAvgStability and the goal document state the missing estimate as a bound on |d log rho_d/dbeta| UNIFORM IN THE LAG AND THE VOLUME, on beta >= 0. CompactBeta rules out the ABSOLUTE bound and is silent on the relative one -- and that silence has been read as OPEN. It is not. REFUTATION ONE, the beta -> 0 end, nothing to do with volume: PowerTail.wilsonCorrAt_at_zero_coupling puts rho_d(0) = 0 at every lag of nonzero circle distance, so a relative bound on an interval STARTING at zero forces rho_d == 0 there (vanishes_of_relative_deriv_bound_from_zero -- Gronwall in the direction needing no integral: rho_d(beta) exp(-K beta) is antitone and starts at zero). With contact_value_pos_at_zero_coupling the forced profile is a POINT MASS. So [beta0, beta1] with beta0 > 0 is the only defensible range, and that costs nothing because ConfinesZero.confines_near_zero already covers a neighbourhood of zero. REFUTATION TWO, the far-lag end, where the VOLUME is the problem: a periodic lattice does not give rho(d) = lam^d -- corr_at_max_lag_eq_lag_one forces lam = 1 and no gap -- the shape is TORUS-SYMMETRIC, rho(n) = lam^n + lam^(M-n), and at the midpoint lag rho = 2 lam^n with rho'/rho = n (lam'/lam) exactly (midpoint_relative_deriv), which grows with the EXTENT (no_uniform_bound_on_torus_profile). The only escape is lam' = 0, a decay rate that does not run with the coupling -- which is what a running gap denies. WHAT SURVIVES: the L1-AGGREGATE form sum_d |rho_d'| <= K sum_d rho_d, with K = |lam'|/(1-lam)^2 carrying NO lag and NO extent (l1_moment_bounded_by_mass); the far-lag terms that blow the per-lag ratio up carry geometrically little mass, and the contact term alone puts the denominator at one -- so NO lower bound on the correlation is needed, which is the scale-freeness CLAY-OUTSTANDING requires. That is why CosAvgStability is built on L1Close and not on a per-lag bound, and th