import MassGap.ApertureRoute  -- THE OBLIGATION IS CONFINEMENT AT ONE FINITE APERTURE. flagship_of_confinement_at_an_aperture: gap, non-triviality, SO(4) and the tight OS0-OS3 continuum limit from ConfinesAtAnAperture alone, which is exists a : EvenAp, forall beta, 3^(-1/4) < cosAvgEven a beta -- stated on the COSINE AVERAGE, not on the tension. That is not cosmetic: Moment.Read.tension is -Real.log of that average and Real.log is EVEN, so log(-1) = 0 and the tension form is satisfied by a read with NO DECAY AT ALL. unguarded_confinement_is_satisfiable_without_decay exhibits it at every aperture -- Substrate.antipodeRead, whose cosine average is exactly -1, and which is the very read the tree uses to show the 1/4 constant cannot be improved and that RP alone leaves the moment unbounded. The read that maximally violates the sufficient condition would have passed the unguarded necessary one. confines_iff_pos_and_tension_lt_floor proves the guarded form equivalent to (0 < cosine average) and (muEven < kappa_0YM), so nothing is strengthened by stating it this way. The substrate hypothesis was only ever consumed through Classical.choose to PICK one aperture -- fullModelEven's four fields take the aperture, not the bound, and the measure side takes nothing -- so the aperture quantifier is DROPPED, not satisfied, and no converse is claimed. That the weakening lost nothing is the theorem flagship_of_substrate_even_via_aperture. It was a definitional identity (Iff.rfl) before the guard; it is not one now, and the reason is benign -- the guarded hypothesis is a different existential, so Classical.choose need not pick the same extent. The conclusion's content is unchanged, only the witness. unguarded_of_confinesAtAnAperture machine-checks that the guard only RESTRICTS the hypothesis. THE EXTENT DOES NOT LOWER THE BAR: in ratio form the criterion is (2pi)^2 * substrateRatio / 2 < 1 - 3^(-1/4) with no N in it, because the aperture cancels EXACTLY (Complete.surplus_ge's hcancel, an equality by field_simp). Choosing the extent buys the QUANTIFIER only -- meet the bar at one extent instead of all of them. Against the unconditional substrateRatio <= 1/4 the sharp threshold substrateThreshold = arccos(3^(-1/4))^2/(2pi)^2 is a factor of 19.7, at EVERY extent. What this does NOT carry: a finite mode count of its own. ymModelEven has Idx := Unit and a mode defined equal to its own bound. The mode count is carried elsewhere and it is derived: SlabQuadratic.wilsonSpectral produces Complete.WilsonSpectral 3 beta at every beta >= 0, through LinkGram.wilsonSpectral_of_quadratic and LagOneDominates.wilsonSpectral_of_pair_and_quadratic, and the witness SpectralFour builds has Idx := Fin 2 -- TWO modes, from the quadratic inequality rather than posted. What that does not give is the bound Aperture.lean's margin wants: PeriodicSpectralForm.hrep reproduces the correlation only at the lags the period resolves, Fin 4 here, so it says nothing about a lag past the aperture.
import MassGap.ReadLayer  -- THE ENTROPTICS READ LAYER, PORTED. The companion development at entroptics/research/lean/Entroptics was CITED by Certify.lean's header as [E, Lem 6.2] and never imported; it pins the same Lean and the same Mathlib rev, so it ported verbatim. tension_eq_log_sub proves the identity Moment.Read.tension's own docstring asserts and nothing proved: tension = log S(0) - log S(2pi/(N+1)), which is exactly the quantity the Weyl-certified band attenuation_weyl_certified propagates. So confines_at_an_aperture_of_certified reaches the flagship's hypothesis from TWO MEASURED NUMBERS AND ONE ERROR BAR rather than from an opaque tension. Also here: resolved_count_certified (the true resolved mode count enclosed by two read-side counts) and the entropy pair, which apply to Moment.Read.p with no adaptation since p is already a probability vector. WHAT IT DOES NOT GIVE, stated because the file is named for the thesis: propagator_recovers_charpoly does NOT produce Complete.WilsonSpectral -- it needs exact noise-free linear dynamics on a state vector and wilsonCorrAt is a Gibbs expectation with no A and no time index, its 'F modes' finiteness is a TYPE fact rather than a derived one, and its conclusion is a charpoly equality which gives neither real eigenvalues nor nonnegative weights nor the two-term shape. Reading-A is a MODELLING ASSUMPTION and Dynamics.lean does not justify it. The Entroptics layer bounds no absolute eigenvalue magnitude anywhere -- every statement is a ratio or a count -- so Aperture.lean's margin stays a hypothesis.
import MassGap.WeakArm  -- THE CONTACT BOUND AT EVERY LAG, and three proved no-gos on reaching the contact-relative quartic law from the coupling-free premises. corrClay_le_at_zero puts rho(d) <= rho(0) at EVERY lag, at even extent with m >= 3 and at EVERY real coupling, given only nonnegativity -- no floor on rho(0), nothing that degrades with the coupling, and invariant under rho -> t*rho. The even lags past the quarter are reached by the circle symmetry corrClay_neg, which turns corrClay_even_antitone's range 2c <= m into c <= m; the ODD lags, which no antitone result reaches because every right-hand lag log-convexity produces is even, are squeezed by corrClay_odd_le between two even neighbours already under rho(0) and the square root taken by nonnegativity -- m >= 3 is exactly the threshold that step needs, not slack. This does NOT contradict odd_scaling_admissible: that no-go forbids a LOWER bound on an odd lag and this is an upper one. wilsonCorrAt_le_at_zero discharges nonnegativity from wilson_reflection_positive_at_even, a theorem and not the named axiom, at the price of 0 <= beta; the conditional form is the one good at every real coupling and the two differ in scope. THE NO-GOS ARE THE OTHER HALF. no_contact_relative_from_shape exhibits, for every constant C and every cut m0, an extent and a profile satisfying MomentShape.Shape AND 0 < rho(0) AND 0 < sum rho -- Shape plus the two further facts available with NO premise depending on the coupling, corrClay_zero_pos (genuinely beta-free) and the second conjunct of the reflection-positivity theorem (every beta >= 0); the same two conjuncts are carried by no_strict_lag_bound_from_shape -- that violates rho(d) <= C*rho(0)/circLag(d)^4 past the cut. The witness is the CONSTANT profile, which is scale-free and carries no floor. no_strict_lag_bound_from_shape is the same witness against a constant factor: no t < 1 gives rho(d) <= t*rho(0) at any lag or extent, so the 1 in Part 1 is OPTIMAL for that premise set and cannot be improved. no_uniform_quartic_constant_of_vanishing_rate is the obstruction where a decay RATE would live: given any family of strictly positive rates with infimum zero, no single C makes e^(-M*k) <= C/k^4 hold across the family at any cut -- the exact complement of StrongArm.exists_geom_quartic_bound, whose S is a function of r, so a constant per rate and no constant for all rates. corrClay_at_period records the index fact the shape argument turns on: on the even-sublattice parameter c in [0,m] the profile g(c) = rho(2c) has g(m) = g(0) because 2m is one period, so the outermost chord of the convex profile is horizontal and gives back exactly Part 1, while every chord that would carry a rate has an interior endpoint whose value log-convexity does not supply. NONE OF THIS SAYS THE QUARTIC LAW IS FALSE of the Wilson correlation -- the tree PROVES it on [0,b] in contact_relative_unconditional. It says the premises that survive at EVERY coupling do not decide it, and names the missing quantity: a decay rate bounded away from one uniformly in the coupling AND the aperture. TWO SCOPE CAVEATS, stated because they are easy to lose: Shape is a COUPLING-FREE premise set -- no premise mentions beta and none carries a beta-dependent constant -- and NOT a coupling-unconditional one, since shape_wilsonCorrAt requires 0 <= beta for its nonneg field; only corrClay_neg and corrClay_log_convex hold at every real beta. Nor is Shape everything the tree proves; and the geometric envelope in the rate no-go is a HYPOTHESIS about an abstract family -- no theorem in this tree derives rho(d)/rho(0) <= e^(-M*d) from corrClay_log_convex, whose log-convexity is the three-point form only. no_uniform_quartic_constant_nonvacuous fires the rate no-go at an exhibited family (invSucc n = 1/(n+1)), so the hypothesis pair is not empty. Foundational only.
import MassGap.HaarVariance  -- THE PURE-HAAR PLAQUETTE VARIANCE, a universal constant with no lattice extent and no coupling in it: haar_variance_reTr_pos gives 0 < Var(Re tr U) under normalized Haar on SU(N) at every N >= 2, and nothing in the statement or the proof mentions a volume, a boundary condition or a beta. The mechanism is PlaqVariance's, run against BARE Haar instead of the Gibbs measure: Re tr is continuous, probHaar is a Haar measure hence IsOpenPosMeasure, so Continuous.ae_eq_iff_eq turns a continuous nonnegative centred square integrating to zero into vanishing at EVERY group element, forcing Re tr globally constant. The gauge-group input is two exhibited elements: the identity reads N, and flipEl = diag(-1,-1,1,...,1) -- determinant (-1)(-1) = 1, so a genuine SU(N) element -- reads N-4, which is where N >= 2 is consumed. THE FOUR-LINK FORM IS REDUCED, NOT ASSUMED: measurePreserving_prod4 proves the ordered product of four independent Haar elements is itself Haar-distributed, and the ONLY invariance it uses is LEFT-invariance (Fubini for the product measure, then measure_preimage_mul collapses the fibre measure to a constant); variance_comp_measurePreserving carries the variance across, so four_link_variance_eq makes the plaquette variance EQUAL to the one-element variance rather than a new constant. The positivity is EXISTENTIAL: it produces no lower bound on the value, only non-vanishing -- which is what a caller reducing an aperture-uniform Wilson-measure bound through an extent-free conditional-density exponent needs, and is why StrongArm's ContactFloor still wants a quantitative floor this does not supply. NEGATIVE CONTROL: haar_variance_reTr_su_one gives EXACTLY 0 at SU(1), where the determinant condition makes the group trivial, so 2 <= N is load-bearing; the witness values were confirmed by asserting the wrong ones and watching the build fail. Foundational only.
import MassGap.CompactBeta  -- THE COUPLING QUANTIFIER SWAP ON A COMPACT INTERVAL, and what it costs. ContactDominance.aperture_uniformity_does_not_give_coupling_uniformity refutes (forall beta, exists B, forall N) -> (exists B, forall N beta) with sepRead; jointUniform_of_pointwise_of_equicontinuous proves the swap IS valid on any COMPACT K given equicontinuity in beta UNIFORM IN THE INDEX, for an arbitrary family of real functions -- a finite subcover of K by delta-balls, the index-uniform bound at each centre, plus epsilon off it. Both hypotheses are load-bearing and both failures are exhibited: spikeFam is pointwise bounded and unbounded over the family on Icc 0 1 (compactness alone gives nothing), rampFam is 1-Lipschitz uniformly in the index and unbounded on univ (equicontinuity alone gives nothing). THE NO-GO SURVIVES INTACT, twice over: sepMoment_jointUniform_on_Icc shows sepRead already meets the new conclusion on EVERY compact interval, capped by ((|a|+|b|+1)/2)^2, so it is a statement about beta -> infinity and nothing else; and sepMoment_not_equicontinuous_on_Icc shows it also fails the new hypothesis on Icc 0 1, with sepMoment_modulus_degrades giving the sharp form -- at aperture 2k+1 the jump is (k+1)^2, so the modulus degrades like N^2. no_go_and_compact_swap_are_compatible states all three together. WHAT THE ROUTE COSTS, and it is not progress: equicontinuousInBeta_of_uniform_lipschitz says the hypothesis is an APERTURE-UNIFORM Lipschitz constant in beta, which via WilsonAnalytic.wilsonSystem_expect_hasDerivAt is a covariance bound uniform in the aperture. clay_covariance_constant_not_aperture_uniform machine-checks that the only UNCONDITIONAL one, cov_bound_extensive's 4*M*#Plaq, is 16(N+1)^4 here because wilsonCorrAt N beta is corrClay (N+1) beta and the aperture IS the extent -- it exceeds every B. The volume-free alternatives (cov_bound_local, cov_bound_summable) take clustering as an argument. AND a volume-free bound on the correlators would still not suffice: profile_to_moment_not_uniformly_lipschitz exhibits, at every L, two reads whose raw profiles differ by at most t at every lag and whose NORMALISED circular second moments differ by more than L*t, the lost factor being ((N+1)/2)^2 -- the probe's own total mass is 1+t, so the amplification is the moment's circLag^2 weight on a lag the aperture has just made available and a floor on the total mass does not touch it. So d2At_jointUniform_on_Icc_of_equicontinuous is stated as the conditional it is. This route relocates the substrate hypothesis from a bound uniform in N and beta to a modulus in beta uniform in N; the second is the clustering estimate the first was waiting on. Foundational only, except the two d2At wrappers, which carry d2At's own footprint.
import MassGap.ConfinesZero  -- B5 AT AND NEAR ZERO COUPLING, AND THE HYPOTHESIS TURNED INTO A NON-EQUALITY. At beta = 0 the connected plaquette correlation vanishes at every nonzero lag (PowerTail.wilsonCorrAt_at_zero_coupling) while the contact value stays positive, so cosAvgEven_at_zero gives cosAvgEven a 0 = 1 EXACTLY -- not a bound -- and confines_at_zero clears the floor 3^(-1/4) at EVERY even aperture. The read clamps at max beta 0, so cosAvgEven_eq_one_of_nonpos extends that to the whole nonpositive half-line; that half-line is the CLAMP, not evidence, and the file says so where it proves it. The moving part is continuity: WilsonAnalytic.wilsonSystem_expect_hasDerivAt differentiates the Gibbs expectation of ANY bounded measurable observable on ANY Wilson system with no hypothesis, and corrClay is three such expectations, so continuous_wilsonSystem_expect / continuous_wilsonCorrConn / continuous_wilsonCorrAt / continuous_cosAvgEven hold at every aperture and every lag with the denominator kept off zero by the second clause of wilson_reflection_positive_at_even. That gives confines_near_zero and confines_below_a_cut: an EXISTENTIAL cut, no numeral. The payoff is confinesAtAnAperture_iff_missesTheFloor -- ConfinesAtAnAperture is EQUIVALENT to MissesTheFloor, exists a, forall beta, cosAvgEven a beta != 3^(-1/4), by the intermediate value theorem against the value 1 at beta = 0. An inequality at every coupling has become a non-equality at every coupling, which is strictly what continuity plus the zero-coupling point buys and nothing more. Two closed forms sharpen the target: cosAvgEven_extent_four = (rho0-rho2)/(rho0+2rho1+rho2), and confines_extent_four_of_lag_two_small reduces the whole hypothesis at extent four, via RP and log-convexity, to rho(2)/rho(0) < ((1-3^(-1/4))/(1+3^(-1/4)))^2 = 0.0186240 -- an EXACT threshold (the discriminant identity ((1-c)rho0-(1+c)rho2)^2 - 4c^2 rho0 rho2 = ((1-c)^2 rho0 - (1+c)^2 rho2)(rho0-rho2) vanishes there by `ring`), NOT a