import MassGap.Hankel  -- THE LAG CORRELATION IS A PSD HANKEL SEQUENCE, AND THAT IS NOT ENOUGH. corrHyper_hankel_psd / corrClay_hankel_psd: the Gram matrix of the Wilson reflection form is positive semidefinite and Hankel (entry (i,j) depends only on i+j, via hankel_lag_val and the circle symmetry of MomentShape.corrHyper_neg), at every real beta and with no positivity hypothesis carried -- the truncated-Hamburger shape the moment problem asks for. It does NOT give a finite mode count. This file is four theorems -- hankel_lag_val, corrHyper_hankel_psd, corrClay_hankel_psd, corrClay_hankel_psd_at_extent_four -- and every one of them is PSD-and-Hankel and nothing further. Curto-Fialkow flat extension is what turns that into a finite mode count, and no declaration in the tree proves flatness. WHAT THE HANKEL SHAPE DOES REACH is a representing measure, and the tree builds it: MomentMeasure.exists_representing_measure for any MomentData, and exists_infinite_volume_representing_measure for the infinite-volume Wilson lag correlator -- nonzero, and supported in [-R, R] -- at every coupling below an existential cut. That measure carries no gap: R arrives as an INPUT through MomentData.shift, from Schwinger.shift_two_le, whose own hypothesis is the geometric decay, so the support bound restates the decay rather than deriving it. The mode count is produced at the Clay aperture by SlabQuadratic.wilsonSpectral, at every beta >= 0, by the quadratic route and not by this one.
import MassGap.Spectral2  -- THE FIRST PRODUCER OF WilsonSpectral, AND ITS LIMIT. wilsonSpectral_at_zero_coupling builds contactForm, a genuine one-mode WilsonSpectral witness with positive weight (contactForm_weight_pos), so the Prop is inhabited rather than merely stated -- but only at beta = 0, where the Wilson measure IS product Haar and wilson_decay_at_zero_coupling has every nonzero lag vanishing identically. The mode is the free point, lambda = 0. This closes the vacuity question about WilsonSpectral and closes nothing about the coupling.
import MassGap.ApertureFamily  -- THE APERTURE QUANTIFIER IS FREE: THE FLAGSHIP SURVIVES THE SWAP WHOLE. flagship_of_confinement_at_each_coupling derives FlagshipAtEach -- gap, non-triviality, SO(4) and the tight OS0-OS3 continuum limit, all four conjuncts -- from ConfinesAtEachCoupling, `forall beta, exists a : EvenAp, 3^(-1/4) < cosAvgEven a beta`, instead of ApertureRoute's `exists a, forall beta`. That is the physically natural form: the aperture is a read aperture at a fixed PHYSICAL scale, so as the lattice refines a fixed physical aperture is a GROWING number of sites, and an aperture that depends on the coupling is what refinement MEANS. The strength was never spent: `LatticeYM.mu` (Model.lean:51) is a BARE FIELD with no requirement to factor as `muEven a` for a fixed a, `A1_YM M = forall beta, M.mu beta < M.kappa0` (Model.lean:69) is pointwise in beta with no cross-coupling clause, `A2_YM` carries no aperture at all, the measure side takes no hypothesis (`measure_is_ymFamilyTension` is `rfl`), and every conjunct of the CONCLUSION has beta outermost. So the only substitution in the whole model is `muEven a` for `tensionOf hc` in three field positions. confinesAtEachCoupling_of_confinesAtAnAperture and flagship_of_confinesAtAnAperture_via_family put the weakening on the record as a weakening. forall_exists_aperture_does_not_give_exists_forall shows the converse is unavailable FROM THE LOGIC (schematic, via `P a beta := beta <= a.1`); it does NOT decide the question for cosAvgEven and the file says so. ContactDominance.aperture_uniformity_does_not_give_coupling_uniformity is NOT about this: the object swapped there is the BOUND B, with the aperture universal on both sides. UniformSurplus names what NEITHER form gives -- `exists Delta > 0, forall beta, Delta <= kappa0YM - mu beta` -- because A1 permits `mu beta` to approach the floor, so the mode magnitude may approach 1 and there is geometric decay at every coupling with no common ratio. 21/21 declarations foundational-only.
import MassGap.ShapeNoGo  -- THE COUPLING-FREE ROUTE IS DEAD, AND IT RESTS ON NO CITED PHYSICS. ShapeFacts collects the five proved shape facts about the lag correlation as one predicate -- nonnegativity with positive total mass, circle symmetry, log-convexity in the lag, even-antitonicity, and the PSD Hankel Gram form, each spelled to match the tree's own statement, with the Hankel clause KEEPING the level map and its `< m` constraint because it is a reflection Gram matrix and the levels must sit below the plane. wilsonCorrAt_shapeFacts discharges all six clauses for the REAL correlator at even extent >= six (`3 <= m`, which is where MomentShape.corrClay_even_antitone stops being vacuous) and `0 <= beta` -- and it is FOUNDATION-ONLY, not carrying wilson_reflection_positive_at, because every clause routes through the proved even-extent forms. Then flatRead, which is literally Moment's own Inhabited witness (`flatRead_eq_default` by rfl), satisfies ShapeFacts at EVERY extent and every m, and flat_cosAvg_eq_zero puts its cosine average at exactly 0 -- four lines over ZeroMode.sum_cos_theta_eq_zero, which already had the root-of-unity sum. So shape_facts_do_not_imply_confinement: the five shape facts together do NOT imply `3^(-1/4) < cosAvg`, since a read satisfying all of them sits at 0. cosAvgEven_eq is `rfl`, so the refuted conclusion is the SAME SCALAR ApertureRoute.ConfinesAtAnAperture bounds, not a paraphrase of it; a primed variant over a bare profile shows it is not an artefact of the Read wrapper. This NARROWS rather than defeats: whatever closes the hypothesis must use the beta-dependence, i.e. the dynamics. Supersedes nothing -- MomentShape.Shape is a three-clause predecessor whose two no-gos are about the PROFILE, where this one is about the CONCLUSION.
import MassGap.MassFinite  -- CLAY ROW B3 -- `m < infinity`, AND IT IS EXACT. clayMass H := sSup {Delta | 0 < Delta and spectrum R H cap Ioo 0 Delta = empty}, Clay's own set. clayMass_concrete = kappa0 and clayMass_ym = DeltaYMAt N beta -- not a bound, the value, so both Clay directions meet on one object. isGreatest_admissibleGaps is the whole argument: an admissible delta > Delta would put Delta inside its own forbidden interval. The step that was missing was the REVERSE spectrum inclusion -- GapOfDecay.mem_spectrum_diagOp had only the subset direction; lam_mem_spectrum_diagOp proves the converse with NO HYPOTHESIS, six lines, because at index k the element algebraMap (lam k) - diagOp lam is zero. What makes it work at all is that cfc_map_spectrum is an EQUALITY of spectra, not a containment: bounding m above needs one EXHIBITED excited state, and an unbounded admissible set is exactly H = 0 on a one-dimensional space, a vacuum and nothing else. Scope, stated in the file: the constructed witnesses, at exactly the strength B1 and B2 hold there.
import MassGap.LocalGauge  -- CLAY ROW A8 -- GAUGE INVARIANCE UNDER THE GENUINE LOCAL GROUP. gaugeTransform g U = fun l => g l.2 * U l * (g (shift l.1 l.2))^{-1}: g at the source site, g^{-1} at the target, using the same `shift` that `bd` traverses with. Every previous gauge statement in the tree was CompactGauge.confConj, a single CONSTANT element conjugating every link -- the global/centre subgroup -- and gaugeTransform_const proves by rfl that confConj is exactly its constant part. hol_gaugeTransform gives conjugation at the base site; the mathematical content is shift_comm, the two far-corner factors cancelling, which IS the statement that the loop closes, and it holds on the diagonal mu = nu too, which matters because Plaq contains it. The measure side came with it: expect_gauge_invariant_local holds for an ARBITRARY observable, because the gauge action is per link a left translation and a right translation and probHaar is invariant under both. corrClay_gauge_invariant_local is the payoff -- an arbitrary g : Site 4 n -> SU 3 substituted into the whole connected correlator.
import MassGap.ReflectionStrong  -- CLAY ROW A4 -- REFLECTION POSITIVITY AT EVERY REAL COUPLING, ON THE EVEN LAGS. wilson_expect_nonneg_module: 0 <= <F.(F o Theta)> on the genuine Wilson Gibbs state for every F in the module of bounded measurable slab observables, with BETA FREE. wilson_expect_gram_nonneg is the PSD GRAM MATRIX over a finite family, and mul_mem_localObs makes that module a unital SUBALGEBRA -- positive semidefiniteness over an algebra, not one observable. Carried to the Clay object by corrClay_nonneg_even_lag at every real beta, with corrClay_nonneg_even_lag_at_negative_coupling witnessing it at beta = -1. WHY THE SIGN CONDITION SURVIVES ON THE ODD LAGS: OddLagSplit.corrClay_reflection_positive is a COMPOSITE of three sources -- even lags from the SITE reflection, where wPlane factors out as a strictly positive weight and a conditional square remains so nothing reads beta's sign; odd lags from the LINK reflection, whose straddling factor IS the Wilson cross kernel; and the positive-mass conjunct from PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos, which is not reflection positivity at all. su3_kernel_nonneg_iff is an iff about that cross kernel only, so it governs the odd-lag route and is silent on the even-lag one -- the two are different objects. wilsonGibbsReflForm is a Transfer.ReflForm on Transfer.reflForm itself with vac_norm discharged.
import MassGap.VolumeRate  -- CLAY ROW B7 -- THE VOLUME-UNIFORM RATE, AND MIXING S1's HYPOTHESIS DERIVED. Every earlier `uniform in volume` conclusion had the shape `exists kappa, 0 < kappa and forall F, Tendsto ...` with kappa ABSENT after the conjunction; exists_pos_and_iff proves that shape equivalent to its own second half, and ym_gap_uniform_in_volume_shape_is_vacuous applies it to the literal conclusion of Complete.ym_gap_uniform_in_volume. gap_rate_uniform_in_volume is the repair: kappa occurs after the conjunction, and gap_rate_at_floor_uniform_in_volume has no existential at all because the rate IS the derived kappa0. The prefactor sum ||P F k|| is given explicitly as a function of F rather than hidden in an exists M -- a volume-dependent amplitude with a volume-INDEPENDENT rate is the meaningful statement, since it is the correlation length 1/kappa that must not grow with the box. product_volume_gap_rate closes the decoupled case with a named rate, its intensive input still DERIVED via product_subvacuum_le. And rp_sub_geometric derives ||T^n x|| <= ||x||.rho1^n on the vacuum-orthogonal subspace from T_symm and T_vac, which is reflection positivity's own payload -- so Mixing S1's hsub is supplied rather than assumed, and the EQUALITY rho'(n) = rho'(1)^n is not needed because every consumer uses the inequality.
