import MassGap.SchwarzIteration  -- T_CONTRACT IS DERIVED FROM T_SYMM, NOT ASSUMED BESIDE IT. TransferData has six fields; two concern the translation's relation to the form. T_SYMM: form_shift_symm proves nu(theta(Tf).g) = nu(theta f.Tg) from ShiftCompat in four rewrites -- the reflection conjugates the forward shift to the backward one, the state is translation-invariant, a translation is multiplicative, and translating back then forward is nothing. That is where reflection positivity earns its keep. T_CONTRACT: contract_of_bounded_orbit derives it. Moving one T across the form and applying Cauchy-Schwarz gives a(n+1)^2 <= a(n) a(n+2) -- midpoint log-convexity of the orbit diagonal -- so if a1 ever exceeded a0 the ratios would be non-decreasing and a(n) would grow geometrically, which a bounded orbit forbids. BOUNDEDNESS IS GENUINELY NEEDED: on A = R with form x y = x y and T x = 2x the form is symmetric and PSD and <Tx,Tx> = 4x^2 > x^2, so 'from symmetry alone' would be FALSE. orbit_bounded_of_state supplies it -- a state is bounded by the sup norm, the sup norm is submultiplicative, and neither reflection nor translation increases it. WHAT IS CONSUMED, NOT ELIMINATED: T_symm itself, as the hypothesis hsym of orbit_log_convex, contract_of_bounded_orbit and null_is_preserved. And ShiftCompat FORCES the translation to be invertible (TransferAssembly.shift_inverse_is_two_sided) -- satisfiable on Z, not on a half-line of N. Nothing here delivers TransferData.T_symm directly; that needs a carrier, which is TransferAssembly's work.
import MassGap.SlabContractive  -- SlabShiftContractive IS NOT AN INDEPENDENT PREMISE. OSPositivity.wilsonSlabTransfer builds a Transfer.TransferData on the Wilson slab algebra from TWO named premises and nothing else, and its docstring says the distance to a transfer operator is exactly those two. IT IS ONE. slabShiftContractive_of_stable derives SlabShiftContractive from SlabShiftStable alone. WHY: contract_of_periodic -- a periodic symmetric map cannot expand a positive semidefinite form. SchwarzIteration.contract_of_bounded_orbit needs T_symm plus a bounded orbit; on the torus the orbit is FINITE, because HalfLineTransfer.shiftObs_pow_period gives shiftObs^n = id, so it visits at most n points and the sup over Finset.range n bounds it (iterate_eq_mod_of_period). No positivity of the operator, no compactness, no spectral theory. The symmetry is already unconditional: WilsonTransfer.reflForm_shiftObs_symm, at every real coupling and every reflection constant, which is what wilsonSlabTransfer already uses for its own T_symm. AND THIS MAKES THE SLAB ROUTE WORSE, NOT BETTER: the surviving premise is SlabShiftStable, and GNSHilbert.shiftSlab_eq_id proves it makes the shift the IDENTITY at 2 <= m, so the operator is 1 whenever the premises hold. Removing a premise from a construction whose surviving premise forces triviality is a SHARPENING OF A NO-GO, not progress toward a gap. What it establishes is that contractivity was never the obstruction -- the whole content of the slab route is the stability premise, which finite_order_fails_gap and shiftObs_eq_self_of_shift_stable between them close.
import MassGap.TransferAssembly  -- A FULL TransferData, EVERY FIELD DISCHARGED, FROM A STATE AND A REFLECTION. assembleTransferData takes a Reflection, an infinite-volume State, the half-space Submodule, reflection-invariance, reflection-POSITIVITY on that submodule, a ShiftCompat, forward-stability of the submodule (HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg_shift_stable), the constant being in it and fixed by the shift, and two sup-norm bounds -- and produces a genuine Transfer.TransferData. T_symm and T_contract are NOT among the inputs: they are proved, by form_shift_symm and contract_of_bounded_orbit fed by orbit_bounded_of_state. restrictT and restrictT_iterate are the carrier bridge, restricting the shift to the submodule and showing the restriction's iterate is the iterate's restriction, which is what lets an orbit bound stated on C(X,R) be read on the submodule. shift_inverse_is_two_sided proves ShiftCompat's hidden consequence: T_S plus theta_T plus involutivity give S . T = id, so the translation is INVERTIBLE on the full algebra -- consistent with the half-space algebra being only FORWARD-stable, and consistent only because the lattice is infinite. THE ONE INPUT THE TREE CANNOT SUPPLY IS hpos: reflection positivity of an infinite-volume Wilson state on the half-space algebra. Everything else on the list is built or is a routine property of precomposition. So this is a REDUCTION of the Yang-Mills transfer operator to ONE hypothesis, with the rest machine-checked -- NOT a construction, and it does not prove the operator exists.
import MassGap.WilsonTransferReduction  -- THE TRANSFER OPERATOR, REDUCED TO THREE FACTS ABOUT THE STATE. TransferAssembly.assembleTransferData takes NINE inputs; SIX are about the lattice and the maps and all six are discharged here. ShiftCompat comes from nu_T alone (shiftCompat_of_nu_T -- the other three fields are ReflectionShift s: ishiftObsL_mul is T_mul, ishiftObsL_iunshiftObs is T_S, ireflObs_ishiftObs is theta_T). hstable is halfSpaceAlg_shift_stable, hone is one_mem_halfSpaceAlg, hTone is ishiftObsL_one, and hTnorm/htheta_norm are norm_comp_le -- precomposition cannot enlarge a supremum, needing no surjectivity. WHAT REMAINS IS EXACTLY THREE, all about the MEASURE: IsReflectionInvariant, ReflPositiveOn on the half-space algebra, and translation invariance of the state. transferData_of_state_facts is the statement. IT SUPPLIES NONE OF THE THREE: WilsonDLR builds an infinite-volume Gibbs MEASURE, not a DLRLimit.State carrying them. ReflPositiveOn IS discharged: ReflectionHalfSpace.reflection_facts_on_halfSpaceAlg returns it together with IsReflectionInvariant for a limit state, and wilson_reflPositive_limit_exists gives it on halfSpaceAlg at every real beta from N != 0 alone. AND IT GIVES NO GAP: even with all three, OpTBridge.reconstruct_from_opT still needs the two spectral hypotheses, which are the mass gap in operator form. This is about the CONSTRUCTION of the operator, not its spectrum -- C1 s operator half was nine obligations of two kinds and is now three of one kind.
import MassGap.WilsonState  -- THE INFINITE-VOLUME WILSON MEASURE, AS A State -- the last piece of plumbing between the Wilson object and the transfer construction. WilsonDLR produces a probability MEASURE on IConf (SU N); WilsonTransferReduction consumes a DLRLimit.State. The tree carried only the other direction (DLRLimit.gibbsMeasure), so the two could not meet. stateOfMeasure is the missing direction and it is integration: nu f = integral of f against P, with the four State fields from integral_add, integral_const_mul, integral_nonneg and measure_univ, and integrability from boundedness on a compact space (integrable_of_continuousMap). AND THE CHAIN CROSSES THE TWO LATTICE SKELETONS: WilsonDLR is written against GibbsSpec s copy of ISite/ILink/IConf and WilsonTransferReduction against InfiniteLattice s. Both are abbrevs over the same underlying types, so they are defeq -- and wilsonTransferData is what CHECKS that rather than asserting it, composing stateOfMeasure into transferData_of_state_facts. WHAT REMAINS: of the three state facts, TWO ARE SUPPLIED -- ReflectionHalfSpace.reflection_facts_on_halfSpaceAlg gives IsReflectionInvariant and ReflPositiveOn on the half-space algebra -- and translation invariance is produced by wilson_nu_T_of_tendsto from the two-family limit identification, so only that identification is conditional, and OpTBridge.reconstruct_from_opT still needs the two spectral hypotheses, which are the mass gap. So every remaining obligation is now a statement about what the Wilson state DOES, none about what object it IS. AND THE LIMIT IS SUBSEQUENTIAL: extracted along an ultrafilter, with no proof the net converges nor that the result is independent of the frozen boundary.
import MassGap.GibbsSpec  -- DLR CONSISTENCY, PROVED, ON THE GENUINE WILSON DENSITY. dlr_consistent: for every Lambda subset Lambda-prime, every measurable f with |f| <= 1 and every boundary configuration omega, gamma_Lambda-prime composed with gamma_Lambda equals gamma_Lambda-prime. The density hypotheses are only Measurable, 0 <= phi and phi <= 2, and nothing about the group beyond Group, MeasurableSpace, MeasurableMul2, MeasurableInv and a probability measure. wilson_dlr_consistent instantiates it at WilsonAction.wilsonDensity on SU(N) against CompactGauge.probHaar at EVERY REAL beta, so the Wilson specification on the infinite lattice IS a specification. The load-bearing lemma is actionBC_split: the boundary action over Lambda-prime splits as the Lambda part plus a remainder evaluated at the OUTSIDE configuration alone, resting on links_not_mem_of_mem_sdiff -- a plaquette touching Lambda-prime but not Lambda reads no link of Lambda. WHY boundaryPlaqs AND NOT plaqsIn, proved rather than asserted: plaqsIn_split_not_local exhibits nested volumes, a plaquette in the difference of their plaqsIn, and a link of that plaquette lying INSIDE Lambda -- so the split lemma's locality hypothesis fails for the free-boundary set. That is the SPLIT failing, not a proof that DLR is false for plaqsIn, and the file says so. boundaryPlaqs_nonempty rules out the other vacuity: a one-link volume already touches a plaquette, so the energy is not a sum over the empty set. ExistsGibbsMeasure and IsGibbsMeasure are DISCHARGED in MassGap.WilsonGibbs; TranslationCovariant remains open.
import MassGap.DLRLimit  -- THE INFINITE-VOLUME GIBBS STATE EXISTS. exists_infinite_volume_gibbs_measure: given a compact, T2, second-countable gauge group, a specification and consistent finite-volume states, there is a PROBABILITY MEASURE ON IConf G whose state satisfies DLR at every finite volume. The economy that makes it cheap: on a compact space, positivity plus normalisation ALONE give |nu f| <= ||f|| (State.abs_le_norm, via State.mono and State.le_norm) with no continuity or boundedness hypothesis, so each coordinate lands in a compact interval fixed by f alone and the compactness needed is one Icc per observable -- Banach-Alaoglu's PROOF specialised to the case where the bound is free, with none of the normed-dual API. exists_limit_state works for ANY NeBot filter on ANY index type with no directedness, countability or metrisability; the four state fields transport by tendsto_nhds_unique and ge_of_tendsto. IsDLR is written on OBSERVABLES, which is where it is a CLOSED condition, so isDLR_of_tendsto is inheritance rather than construction. borelSpace_iconf is where countability of ILink is spent: over an uncountable index the product sigma-algebra is strictly smaller than the Borel one and Gibbs measure would name a different object. NON-TRIVIALITY IS SIZED RATHER THAN CLAIMED: nu 1 = 1 is a FIELD and rules out the zero functional and nothing else; point-mass exclusion is proved CONDITIONALLY on a variance floor holding UNIFORMLY in the volume, and GibbsPositive.corrNum_plaqObs_pos is NOT that floor -- it bounds a correlation at a FIXED volume and a correlation is not a variance. gamma carries the FELLER property in its type (continuous functions to continuous functions), which GibbsSpec proves measurability but not continuity of -- put there deliberately so it cannot be skipped silently.
import MassGap.InfiniteReflection  -- REFLECTION POSITIVITY IS NOT LOST IN THE THERMODYNAMIC LIMIT. A TransferData on the infinite lattice needs form_nonneg, which is reflection positivity, and at finite volume that is the named axiom wilson_reflection_positive_at. This asks whether the LIMIT costs anything beyond it. FIRST, THE RESTRICTION IS NOT OPTIONAL: reflection_positivity_fails_off_the_half_space proves that 0 <= nu(theta F . F) is FALSE for all observables -- whenever theta F = -F, as for an antisymmetric observable, it reads -nu(F.F) < 0 -- so the condition is asserted ON A SUBMODULE (ReflPositiveOn), which is exactly why ReflectStrong.wilsonGibbsReflForm is carried on localObs (blkS) (blkR) and not on the whole Wilson algebra. Stating it unrestricted would make every theorem here vacuous. THE TRANSPORT: DLRLimit.le_of_eventually_le passes a uniform lower bound to the limit, and RP is one at c = 0, so reflPositive_of_tendsto is that lemma once per observable and isReflectionInvariant_of_tendsto is uniqueness of limits. NO NEW AXIOM. THE FORM: stateReflForm builds a genuine Transfer.ReflForm on the submodule from four properties of the reflection plus invariance and positivity, so GNSHilbert's space, vacuum and operator lift all apply; stateReflForm_vac_norm settles TransferData.vac_norm when the constant is in the submodule. BRACKETED BOTH WAYS: trivialReflection_positive_always shows theta = id makes the condition empty, and the failure theorem shows dropping the submodule makes it false -- the content is entirely in which submodule is chosen. NOT DELIVERED: no state is shown to satisfy it, so these are theorems ABOUT a hypothesis.
import MassGap.OSPositivity  -- CLAY ROW A4 -- OS POSITIVITY, AND THE POSITIVITY ITSELF IS NO LONGER WHAT SEPARATES US FROM OS3. Two of the six separations ReflectionStrong named are closed here. SESQUILINEARITY: Mathlib has no complexification of a real PSD bilinear form, so cform is built on Transfer.PreForm with conjugate symmetry, conjugate-linear left and linear right, real diagonal and the COMPLEX Gram cform_gram_re_nonneg / cform_gram_im_zero at complex coefficients and complex test vectors. It is not an analogue: cform_eq_osPairing proves cform at the pair of parts of F, G IS the Gibbs expectation of conj(F o Theta) . G componentwise, which needed EW additivity discharged from localObs's own bound. So wilson_osC_diag_re_nonneg gives 0 <= <conj(F o Theta) . F> at BETA FREE and wilson_osC_diag_im_zero gives that the pairing is REAL -- together OS3's inequality in full. THE ALGEBRA CLAUSE: prod_mem_localObs extends to arbitrary finite products and wilson_gram_nonneg_monomials is the combination -- the Gram matrix over the MONOMIALS in any family of slab generators is PSD, i.e. positive semidefiniteness over the generated unital subalgebra rather than over a subspace. What still separates the tree from OS3 is the slab/half-space geometry, the limits, the link reflections and the other OS axioms. Free bonus: Transfer.GNS at wilsonGibbsReflForm is already a genuine InnerProductSpace R -- slab_inner_mk and slab_vac_norm give the Hilbert space and a UNIT VACUUM at finite volume on the slab, today. wilsonSlabTransfer builds a COMPLETE TransferData from exactly two named Props, SlabShiftStable and SlabShiftContractive, every other field being a theorem at every real beta -- and SlabShiftStable is very likely FALSE, since HalfLineTransfer.const_of_shift_stable makes any submodule satisfying it consist of constants.
import MassGap.PlaqCount  -- THE COUPLING CONVENTION, AS AN IDENTITY. WilsonHypercubic.Plaq is an ORDERED direction pair, so ((mu,nu),x) and ((nu,mu),x) are distinct elements and both enter every sum over plaquettes. hol_swap gives that the two orderings have INVERSE holonomies, wilsonDensity_hol_swap that they therefore have EQUAL Wilson density (Re tr is inversion-blind on SU(N)), and wilsonDensity_hol_diag that the mu = nu diagonal contributes zero. sum_pair_eq_two_mul_lt is the Finset combinatorics -- symmetric plus diagonal-zero means the ordered sum is twice the mu < nu sum -- and plaq_ordered_double_counts states it. The payoff is boltz_eq_std: (sysWilson N d n).boltz beta U = exp(-(2 beta) . sum over mu < nu of phi_W), i.e. beta_Lean = beta_standard / 2 as a MACHINE-CHECKED IDENTITY rather than a reading. The Re tr half already existed as OddLagSplit.re_tr_hol_swap, general in d, n and N; what was missing was the counting consequence. Nothing in PAPER.md, in certify/ or in the data is wrong because of this: every MEASURED beta in the tree is the standard Wilson coupling, fixed by lattice_generator summing over nu in range(mu+1, D) and held there by test_generator_physics against Montvay-Munster, Creutz and the weak-coupling limit. The ordered-Plaq beta lives only inside the Lean development, which pins no numeric coupling anywhere.
import MassGap.WilsonDLR  -- CLAY ROW A6 -- AN INFINITE-VOLUME GIBBS MEASURE FOR THE WILSON THEORY. exists_wilson_infinite_volume_gibbs_measure: for every N != 0 and EVERY REAL beta there is a probability measure P on IConf (SU N) with integral of spec wilsonDensity beta Lambda probHaar f against P equal to the integral of f, at every finite volume and every continuous f. No coupling regime, no volume bound, no smallness condition; the density is the real 1 - Re tr U / N, the measure is probHaar, and the plaquette set is boundaryPlaqs so the conditioning is a genuine boundary condition. THE FELLER PROPERTY IS WHAT THIS CLOSES: DLRLimit's gamma demands continuous to continuous and GibbsSpec proved only measurability. continuous_spec_right gets it from MeasureTheory.continuous_of_dominated -- spec is num/part, both integrals over a finite product of copies of G of an integrand continuous in omega and dominated by a CONSTANT, the constant free because IConf G is compact by Tychonoff, and part_pos keeping the quotient continuous. FirstCountableTopology on the parameter space comes from ILink being countable. isLocalOn_spec and spec_mem_localAlg give the locality half, so gamma lands in C(X,R) legitimately rather than by fiat. ONE OBSTRUCTION HAD TO BE REMOVED FIRST: GibbsSpec.DLRConsistent quantifies only over f with |f| <= 1, while DLRLimit's hcons quantifies over ALL continuous f, and a continuous function on a compact space is bounded but not by 1 -- spec_smul (exact homogeneity, needing only integral_const_mul) rescales by (C+1) inverse and dlr_general is the result. WHAT THIS DOES NOT GIVE, and the file says so: the DLR equation holds against CONTINUOUS observables, not all bounded measurable ones, so GibbsSpec.IsGibbsMeasure is claimed in MassGap.WilsonGibbs, by a MEASURE-level argument rather than the density one predicted here -- gibbsMeasure is a Riesz-Markov representative and extending needs a monotone-class argument, which is self-contained measure theory rather than another Feller-sized hole. Also not proved and inherited from DLRLimit: uniqueness, translation invariance, and non-degeneracy -- the limit is along an ultrafilter refining atTop, so it is subsequential and may depend on the frozen boundary configuration.
import MassGap.SpecVarianceFloor  -- PART IV WITHOUT THE TRANSPORT. clay_four_parts takes hvar directly, with the observable, the boundary condition and the constant all the caller's, so a variance floor proved on Z^4 discharges Part IV with no comparison to the periodic torus anywhere in it -- the bridge route clay_nontriviality_of_eventual_wilson_bridge is one way to hvar, not the only one, and its universal form is refuted by VarianceBridge.wilson_bridge_hypothesis_unsatisfiable. THE MOVE: read one link and cut the action at boundaryPlaqs of that single link, which does not depend on the region once the link is in it, so a bound in its cardinality carries no volume; every region-indexed cut leaves a factor whose plaquette count grows, which is why BoxNumericFloor's floor dies as the box grows. The remaining factor is never evaluated -- it is common to numerator and denominator and goes by the inequality part <= integral of rest, as ContactFloor does on the torus. GibbsSpec and ActionSplit do not import one another; ReflectionHalfSpace already uses both, and what is new here is GibbsSpec.spec against ActionSplit.block_factor in particular.
import MassGap.WilsonGibbs  -- CLAY ROW A6, FINISHED: GibbsSpec.IsGibbsMeasure HOLDS FOR THE WILSON SPECIFICATION AT EVERY REAL BETA. exists_wilson_isGibbsMeasure (N != 0) (beta : R) gives a probability measure P with the DLR equation at every finite volume and every BOUNDED MEASURABLE f, not merely every continuous one -- and since the sigma-algebra is the full Borel one, that is strictly more observables and real content. wilson_dlr_bounded_measurable writes it out, and that it typechecks as a term application of the bundled form is itself the proof that IsGibbsMeasure resolves to GibbsSpec's and not a lookalike. THE DENSITY ROUTE DOES NOT WORK AND IS NOT USED: abs_spec_le bounds the kernel by the SUP norm of the observable, not by its L1(P) norm, and the kernel integrates f against a DIFFERENT measure for each boundary configuration -- so L1 convergence says nothing about the kernel and the equation does not transfer. spec_smul does not rescue it: the obstruction is the wrong norm, not the wrong radius. What works is MEASURE-LEVEL and approximates no observable anywhere. specMeasure is the kernel applied to P as a measure in its own right, a pushforward along the splice of P tensor vol weighted by wt/part; integral_specMeasure equates it to the kernel integral for EVERY bounded measurable f at once by Fubini; specMeasure_eq_self then uses WilsonDLR's CONTINUOUS equation plus MeasureTheory.ext_of_forall_integral_eq_of_IsFiniteMeasure to conclude the two measures are EQUAL, and the bounded-measurable statement is one reading of the first rewritten by the second. The one genuinely new estimate is exp_neg_escale_le_part: part bounded below UNIFORMLY in omega, which GibbsSpec.part_pos does not give since it is positive at each omega separately while the boundary condition is one of the two integration variables. The metrisability HasOuterApproxClosed needs costs no new hypothesis: IConf G is a product of topological groups hence a topological group hence regular, and second countable because ILink is countable, so Urysohn closes it -- note pseudoMetrizableSpace_pi is [Finite]-only in this Mathlib and would not have served. escale uses |beta|, so both signs are covered. Still open and inherited from WilsonDLR: uniqueness, translation invariance, and non-degeneracy -- the limit is subsequential and may depend on the anchoring boundary configuration. Also carries gibbsSpec_plaqsIn_eq, the bridge between the two plaqsIn that are extensionally equal and not defeq.
import MassGap.SliceTrace  -- Z = Tr(T^n), PROVED, AS A CYCLIC KERNEL INTEGRAL. partition_eq_cycleIntegral: the Wilson partition function is the integral over slab configurations of the product over t of slabKernel t (W t) (W (t+1)). CYCLICITY IS TYPE-ENFORCED, not notational: slabKernel t has second argument type indexed by t+1, so the wrap from slab n-1 back to slab 0 cannot be broken and still typecheck. The content is slabWeight_local -- the slab weight genuinely reads only the links at times t and t+1, via ReflectionPositivity.action_on_congr_of_support applied to SliceTransfer.intra_links_mem and inter_links_mem -- and the degenerate plaquette ((tau,tau),x) is removed by THEOREM (interSliceAction_eq_nondeg), which is why hN : N != 0 is carried throughout. THE MATHLIB GAP IT FILLED: v4.31.0 has MeasurableEquiv.piCurry and the Ionescu-Tulcea infinitePi_map_piCurry, but NO measurePreserving_piCurry for Measure.pi -- that single absence was the whole obstruction, confirmed by grepping the pinned checkout rather than recalled. measurePreserving_sigmaUncurry proves it from Measure.pi_eq on rectangles plus Finset.prod_sigma, and measurePreserving_confEquiv is the general block regrouping for any c : iota -> kappa out of a fintype -- OddLagSplit.join3 / integral_three_block generalised from three blocks to an arbitrary finite index. WHY AN ITERATED INTEGRAL RATHER THAN A trace: T acts on L2 of a continuum probability space, Matrix.trace needs an index type, LinearMap.trace is a dite on a finite basis and returns 0 when there is none, and Mathlib v4.31.0 carries NO Schatten, Hilbert-Schmidt or trace-class machinery at all -- so there is no Tr to prove this equal to and naming it as the integral is a definition rather than an approximation. twoSlab_expect is the payoff, the integral form of Tr(Phi T^d Psi T^{n-d}) / Tr(T^n). LOCALITY IS SHARP FROM n >= 3 AND VACUOUS BELOW: slabSupport_eq_univ_iff proves slabSupport = univ iff n <= 2, both directions, and at n = 1 slabKe