import MassGap.SpectralBound  -- WHERE B5 ACTUALLY STANDS, AND TWO CORRECTIONS. FIRST, THE THRESHOLD IN THE EIGENVALUE VARIABLE HAS A CLOSED FORM AND MY NUMERAL FOR IT WAS UNSAFE: lambdaThreshold = (1 - 3^{-1/4})/(1 + 3^{-1/4}), and lambdaThreshold_sq proves its square IS lagTwoThreshold by rfl, no root extracted because lagTwoThreshold was already a square. Its value is 0.1364697376..., so 0.13647 is that ROUNDED UP and does NOT give the criterion -- confines_of_lag_two_ratio needs a STRICT inequality. The largest five-digit numeral that works is 0.136469, and confines_of_subdominant_le is stated there. floor_sq_tight and floor_tight re-derive 3^{-1/4} in (0.7598356, 0.759836) for it; only the lower digit is new. SECOND, AND LARGER: spectralAt_iff proves SpectralAt beta Lambda IFF (0 <= Lambda and rho(2) <= Lambda^2 rho(0)), at every real coupling, the backward direction taking one weight and one eigenvalue -- so THE SPECTRAL FRAMING IS A RELABELLING OF THE SAME INEQUALITY, not a second route. B5 at the smallest even aperture needs no Z = Tr(T^n), no spectral decomposition, and no weights coming from an operator. It works because the tree already has both halves unconditionally in beta: PlaqVariance.corrClay_zero_pos for rho(0) > 0 and ReflectionStrong.corrClay_nonneg_even_lag for 0 <= rho(2) at the EVEN lag two, where reflection positivity carries no sign condition. THE CLUSTER-EXPANSION ROUTE IS VOLUME-INDEPENDENT AND STILL CANNOT REACH A TAIL: coreRate and coreConst take only (K, beta) with no extent, and the ratio constant is NOT contact_relative_constant_too_large's constant in disguise since it carries a coreRate factor that vanishes at beta = 0 -- but expansion_domain_bounded proves there is a B with 1 < coreRate (16*4) beta for every beta >= B, so the hypothesis corrClay_abs_le_coreConst_mul_rate_pow literally carries is FALSE on a whole half-line, and the crossover is outside the domain of convergence. THE DOEBLIN ROUTE IS REFUTED AS A THEOREM RATHER THAN 